  "description": "Oatmeal adds a wholesome flavor and an interesting texture to this banana bread, and there are no wet chunks of banana in the bread because the wet ingredients are mixed in the blender. You still get the moisture, sweetness and most importantly flavor from the bananas.",
  "notes": "Notes: Make sure your bananas are at least very ripe, or overripe. You can even use frozen bananas, if you allow them to thaw and come to room temperature first (cold bananas will make the batter cold and the bread will take longer to bake).\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Tightly wrapped, the bread can be refrigerated for 3-5 days or frozen for up to 1 month.",
